    "title": "What channel is Florida basketball vs Iowa on today? How to watch March Madness game",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 11:15 a.m. ETFlorida basketball is set to face Iowa for its next matchup in March Madness.Top-seeded UF (27-7) will now face No. 9 Iowa on Sunday, March 22, at Benchmark International Arena in Tampa.The Hawkeyes (22-10) defeated No. 8 Clemson 67-61 after Bennett Stirtz led Iowa with a team-high 16 points.Florida went on a 43-6 run in the first half against No. 16 Prairie View A&M to cruise to a 114-55 win in its opening-round game of the tournament.Florida set a new program record with its sixth 100-point game of the season. It also marks UF’s third 100-point game all-time in NCAA Tournament play and the Gators’ most points in an NCAA Tournament game.This is Florida’s 26th appearance in the NCAA tournament, which includes its vacated seasons, while Iowa is making its 30th appearance.Buy Florida basketball NCAA tournament ticketsHow to watch Florida basketball vs IowaStream: SlingChannel: TBSFlorida vs will be televised on TBS and can be streamed on Sling, which day pass to those who aren't subscribed. Tom McCarthy, Dan Bonner and AJ Ross will be on the call at Benchmark International Arena.Stream Florida basketball vs Iowa on SlingWhat time does Florida basketball vs Iowa tipoff?Date: Sunday, March 22Time: 7:10 p.m. E.T.Florida basketball 2025-26 scheduleGame 1: Arizona 93, Florida 87Game 2: Florida 104, North Florida 64Game 3: Florida 78, Florida State 76Game 4: Florida 82, Miami 68Game 5: Florida 80, Merrimack 40Game 6: TCU 84, Florida 80Game 7: Florida 90, Providence 78Game 8: Duke 67, Florida 66Game 9: UConn 77, Florida 73Game 10: Florida 80, George Washington 70Game 11: Florida 102, St. Francis 61Game 12: Florida 90, Colgate 60Game 13: Florida 94, Dartmouth 72Game 14: Missouri 76, Florida 74Game 15: Florida 92, Georgia 77Game 16: Florida 91, Tennessee 67Game 17: Florida 96, Oklahoma 79Game 18: Florida 98, Vanderbilt 94Game 19: Florida 79, LSU 61Game 20: Auburn 76, Florida 67Game 21: Florida 95, South Carolina 48Game 22: Florida 100, Alabama 77Game 23: Florida 86, Texas A&M 67Game 24: Florida 86, Georgia 66Game 25: Florida 92, Kentucky 83Game 26: Florida 76, South Carolina 62Game 27: Florida 94, Ole Miss 75Game 28: Florida 84, Texas 71Game 29: Florida 111, Arkansas 77Game 30: Florida 108, Mississippi State 74Game 31: Florida 84, Kentucky 77Game 32: Florida 71, Kentucky 63Game 33: Vanderbilt, 91, Florida 74Game 34: Florida 114, Prairie View A&M 55NCAA Tournament Second Round March 22Reach Florida Gators writer Andrew Abadie at AAbadie@usatodayco.com or on X (formerly Twitter) at @AndrewAbadie. You can also find him on Facebook at Andrew Abadie Sports Reporter or on Instagram @andrewabadie_sports.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
